  #line-at(72pt, 269.66pt, "Abstract: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(123.5pt, 269.66pt, "Two-dimensional (2D) semiconductors such as molybdenum disulfide (MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(489.94pt, 270.14pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(493.96pt, 269.66pt, ") have ")
  #line-at(72pt, 290.36pt, "recently attracted extensive research attention due to their promising compatibility with silicon-")
  #line-at(72pt, 311.06pt, "based electronics. However, several key challenges still limit their practical integration. Two ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.76pt, "of the critical issues are: (1) the intrinsic depletion-mode (normally-on) operation of MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(519.28pt, 332.24pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 352.46pt, "field-effect transistors (FETs), and (2) the large hysteresis commonly observed in the transfer ")
  #line-at(72pt, 373.16pt, "characteristics of MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(181.04pt, 373.64pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(185.06pt, 373.16pt, " FETs due to the inherent sulfur defects. Addressing them is essential ")
  #line-at(72pt, 393.86pt, "for CMOS-compatible 2D-transistor technologies. In this work, we report for the first time that ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.56pt, "surface modification of the exfoliated multilayer MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(343.18pt, 415.04pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(347.2pt, 414.56pt, " FETs with PBTTT-C14 (poly(2,5-")
  #line-at(72pt, 435.26pt, "bis(3-tetradecylthiophen-2-yl)thieno[3,2-b]thiophene)), a p-type conjugated organic polymer, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 455.96pt, "converts the device from depletion-mode to enhancement-mode operation while ")
  #line-at(72pt, 476.66pt, "simultaneously and strongly suppressing hysteresis. Specifically, the threshold voltage (V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(513.22pt, 477.14pt, "th")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(519.4pt, 476.66pt, ") ")
  #line-at(72pt, 497.38pt, "shifts from −9.6 V to +5.9 V (total shift ~15.5 V), and the hysteresis window decreases from ")
  #line-at(72pt, 518.08pt, "8.8 V to 1.3 V (~85% reduction). This originates from interfacial charge transfer at the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 538.78pt, "MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.34pt, 539.26pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(99.36pt, 538.78pt, "/PBTTT-C14 interface, enabled by favourable band alignment. Additionally, donor-like ")
  #line-at(72pt, 559.48pt, "sulfur vacancy states in MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(210.68pt, 559.96pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(214.7pt, 559.48pt, " are involved in interfacial charge transfer to the p-type PBTTT-")
  #line-at(72pt, 580.12pt, "C14 layer, resulting in effective deactivation of these donor states associated with the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 600.82pt, "generation of free charge carriers and hysteresis. Importantly, this highlights the role of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 621.52pt, "electronic interaction at the interface. To further validate this charge-transfer-driven ")
  #line-at(72pt, 642.22pt, "mechanism, P3HT (poly(3-hexylthiophene-2,5-diyl)) with similar energy levels to PBTTT-")
  #line-at(72pt, 662.92pt, "C14 was employed, and it also showed similar enhancement-mode behaviour and hysteresis ")
  #line-at(72pt, 683.62pt, "suppression. In contrast, treatment with a n-type polymer (N2200)  (poly{[N,N′-bis(2-")
  #line-at(72pt, 704.32pt, "octyldodecyl)-naphthalene-1,4,5,8-bis(dicarboximide)-2,6-diyl]-alt-5,5′-(2,2′-bithiophene)})  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 725.02pt, "with less favourable band alignment which limits interfacial charge transfer, resulted in a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 745.72pt, "smaller V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(118.7pt, 746.2pt, "th")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(124.94pt, 745.72pt, " shift from −13.8 V to −8.3 V (total shift of ~5.5 V) without inducing enhancement-")
