  #line-at(519.4pt, 428.36pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 448.58pt, "FETs with p-type organic polymers PBTTT-C14 and P3HT enables simultaneous (1) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 469.28pt, "modulation of threshold voltage (V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(249.74pt, 469.76pt, "th")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(255.98pt, 469.28pt, ") and (2) strong hysteresis suppression. Coating with ")
  #line-at(72pt, 489.98pt, "PBTTT-C14 shifted V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(179.78pt, 490.46pt, "th")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(186.02pt, 489.98pt, " from –9.6 V to +5.9 V, effectively converting normally-on, depletion-")
  #line-at(72pt, 510.7pt, "mode (D-mode) devices into enhancement-mode (E-mode) operation and reducing hysteresis ")
  #line-at(72pt, 531.4pt, "from 8.8 V to 1.3 V (~85%). This behaviour originates from interfacial charge transfer at the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 552.1pt, "MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(95.34pt, 552.58pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(99.36pt, 552.1pt, "/polymer interface, driven by favourable energy-level alignment. Consistently, P3HT ")
  #line-at(72pt, 572.8pt, "with comparable energy level to PBTTT-C14, produced similar modulation, whereas the n-")
  #line-at(72pt, 593.5pt, "type polymer N2200 induced modest V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(262.22pt, 593.98pt, "th")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(268.46pt, 593.5pt, " shifts from –13.8 V to +8.3 V, without converting to ")
  #line-at(72pt, 614.2pt, "E-mode operation and hysteresis from 11.2 V to 5.6 V (~50%), underscoring the critical role ")
  #line-at(72pt, 634.9pt, "of polymer-MoS")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(151.7pt, 635.38pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(155.72pt, 634.9pt, " energy-level alignment. Control experiments using insulating PDMS showed ")
  #line-at(72pt, 655.6pt, "no significant change in V")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.98pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(196.28pt, 656.08pt, "th")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(202.52pt, 655.6pt, " and hysteresis, further confirming that mere physical encapsulation ")
  #line-at(72pt, 676.3pt, "is insufficient and electronic interaction at the interface is essential. The reproducibility and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 697pt, "stability of these effects were validated across multiple devices. Overall, our findings establish ")
  #line-at(72pt, 717.7pt, "that tailored organic–inorganic heterostructures provide a robust strategy for V")
